<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Fixlet>
    <Title>SYM16-015 - Symantec Endpoint Protection 12.1 - Target Versions earlier than 12.1.6 MP5 (x64)</Title>
    <Description><![CDATA[
<TABLE><TBODY><TR><TD> <P>This sample Fixlet&nbsp;updates&nbsp;Symantec Endpoint Protections with version&nbsp;earlier than&nbsp;12.1.6.MP5&nbsp;in&nbsp;response to the advisory&nbsp;SYM16-015.</P> <P><STRONG>Note:</STRONG> The patch must be manually cached for it to run correctly. For more information on how to manually cache files, see <A href="http://www-01.ibm.com/support/docview.wss?uid=swg21506037">this technote </A>.<BR><BR></P> <P>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;This Fixlet does not have a default action because additional preparation is required before deployment. For more information on default actions, see <A href="http://support.bigfix.com/cgi-bin/kbdirect.pl?id=474">this technote</A>.</P> <P></STRONG>To deploy the fixlet successfully,&nbsp;follow the instructions below: </P> <P>1. 1. Find the current installed Symantec Endpoint Protection build number by using the following relevance in the Fixlet Debugger tool:&nbsp;&nbsp;<BR>Q: value "PRODUCTVERSION" of key "HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Symantec\Symantec Endpoint Protection\CurrentVersion" of native&nbsp;registry.<BR>The queried answer provides the version number of the product. For example,A: 12.1.5337.5000. The build number is 5337</P> <P><STRONG>Note:</STRONG> To use the Fixlet Debugger tool, run the FixletDebugger.exe file, which is located in Program Files &gt; BigFix Enterprise &gt; BES Console &gt; QnA. For more information about the Fixlet Debugger, see <A href="http://www.ibm.com/support/knowledgecenter/SS6MER_9.5.0/com.ibm.bigfix.doc/Platform/Relevance/c_using_the_fixlet_debugger.html">Using the Fixlet Debugger tool</A>.</P> <P>2. Download&nbsp;respective patch from <A href="https://support.symantec.com/en_US/article.INFO3931.html">Symantec article&nbsp;page</A>.</P> <P>3. Extract&nbsp;the patch files and find corresponging installer for current&nbsp;product&nbsp;version.+ For example, if the&nbsp;current build version is 5337, the installation file&nbsp;would be&nbsp;Sep64_5337To7061_clientDAXMSI.exe</P> <P>4. Use the Fixlet Debugger tool to calculate the sha1, size, and sha256 values of the installer. For example, use the following relevance: Q: (sha1 of it, size of it, sha256 of it) of file "C:\Users\ADMIN\Downloads\SEP_To_7061\Sep64_5337To7061_clientDAXMSI.exe".</P> <P>5. Update the Fixlet action to use the queried values of the sha1, size, and sha256 properties. Use the same sha1 value in the 'action may require restart' command.</P> <P>6. Rename the installer file with the sha1 value. For example, if the sha1 value is ebd5b025c5c7f1c3608ec3e5000ecd27181c00bd, rename the "Sep64_5337To7061_clientDAXMSI.exe" file to "ebd5b025c5c7f1c3608ec3e5000ecd27181c00bd".</P> <P>7. Place the renamed installer file in the BES Server download cacher folder. For more information about manually caching file downloads on the BES Server, see <A href="http://www-01.ibm.com/support/docview.wss?uid=swg21506037">this technote</A>.<BR></P> <P>&nbsp;</P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE>
]]></Description>
    <Relevance>if( name of operating system starts with &quot;Win&quot; ) then platform id of operating system != 3 else false</Relevance>
    <Relevance><![CDATA[exist value "PRODUCTVERSION" whose ( it as string as version < "12.1.7004.6500") of key "HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Symantec\Symantec Endpoint Protection\CurrentVersion" of native registry]]></Relevance>
    <Relevance>(not ia64 of operating system) and (x64 of operating system)</Relevance>
    <Relevance><![CDATA[not exist value "PRODUCTVERSION" whose ( it as string as version >= "12.1.7061.6600") of key "HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Symantec\Symantec Endpoint Protection\CurrentVersion" of native registry]]></Relevance>
    <Category>Security Update</Category>
    <SourceReleaseDate>2016-10-05</SourceReleaseDate>
    <MIMEField>
    	<Name>x-fixlet-modification-time</Name>
    	<Value>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 22:01:52 +0000</Value>
    </MIMEField>
    <Domain>BESC</Domain>
    <Action ID="Action22900">
      <Description>
        <PreLink>Click </PreLink>
        <Link>here</Link>
        <PostLink>to execute this action.</PostLink>
      </Description>
      <ActionScript MIMEType="application/x-Fixlet-Windows-Shell">prefetch Sep64_5337To7061_clientDAXMSI.exe sha1:ebd5b025c5c7f1c3608ec3e5000ecd27181c00bd size:21647920  https://MANUAL_BES_CACHING_REQUIRED/Sep64_5337To7061_clientDAXMSI.exe sha256:b138ef8defc0f9c92ed93925f75b0e16270acaedfe4d5812cbf635f1ea2fad54

waithidden __Download\Sep64_5337To7061_clientDAXMSI.exe

action may require restart &quot;ebd5b025c5c7f1c3608ec3e5000ecd27181c00bd&quot;</ActionScript>
    </Action>
    <Action ID="Action22901">
      <Description>
        <PreLink>Click </PreLink>
        <Link>here</Link>
        <PostLink>for more information about solutions for SYM16-015.</PostLink>
      </Description>
      <ActionScript MIMEType="text/x-uri">https://support.symantec.com/en_US/article.INFO3900.html</ActionScript>
    </Action>
  </Fixlet>
</BES>
